#: ai/pantoken-ai/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/ai` — consumer-facing agent assets for projects that *use* "
"pantoken (not for\n"
"developing pantoken itself)."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/ai` — consumer-facing agent assets for projects that *use* "
"pantoken (not for\n"
"developing pantoken itself)."

#: ai/pantoken-ai/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"It ships an `AGENTS.md`, an `llms.txt`, editor/agent rule files (Cursor, "
"Copilot, Windsurf), and\n"
"Claude Code skills (`init-pantoken`, `create-pantoken-app`), plus "
"[installAgentAssets](functions/installAgentAssets.md) /\n"
"[scaffoldAndInit](functions/scaffoldAndInit.md) / the `pantoken-ai` CLI to "
"drop them into a consumer repo at the\n"
"conventional paths."
msgstr ""
"It ships an `AGENTS.md`, an `llms.txt`, editor/agent rule files (Cursor, "
"Copilot, Windsurf), and\n"
"Claude Code skills (`init-pantoken`, `create-pantoken-app`), plus "
"[installAgentAssets](functions/installAgentAssets.md) /\n"
"[scaffoldAndInit](functions/scaffoldAndInit.md) / the `pantoken-ai` CLI to "
"drop them into a consumer repo at the\n"
"conventional paths."

#: ai/pantoken-ai/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Asset content and the writer function now live in `@pantoken/scaffold` (so "
"the base scaffold\n"
"flow can offer them without a circular dependency); re-exported here for "
"back-compat."
msgstr ""
"Asset content and the writer function now reside in `@pantoken/scaffold` (so "
"the base scaffold\n"
"flow can offer them without a circular dependency); re-exported here for "
"backwards compatibility."

