#: css/wrapper.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`body[class~=\"instui-display-flex\"]` — App-shell row: side nav, container "
"with header, and optional panel."
msgstr ""
"`body[class~=\"instui-display-flex\"]` — App-shell row: side nav, container "
"with header, and optional panel."

#: css/wrapper.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Wrapper when:"
msgstr "✅ Use Wrapper when:"

#: css/wrapper.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- Building a full Canvas product page that needs a consistent layout shell\n"
"- The page uses GlobalNav as the primary navigation anchor\n"
"- The page needs side panels: ContentTabList, TrailingContentArea, or a "
"UtilityPanel\n"
"- You need consistent container padding and content max-width across the "
"full page\n"
"🚫 Don't use Wrapper when:"
msgstr ""
"- Building a full Canvas product page that needs a consistent layout shell\n"
"- The page uses GlobalNav as the primary navigation anchor\n"
"- The page needs side panels: ContentTabList, TrailingContentArea, or a "
"UtilityPanel\n"
"- You need consistent container padding and content max-width across the "
"full page\n"
"🚫 Don't use Wrapper when:"

#: css/wrapper.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- Building a Modal, Tray, or Drawer — those have their own layout "
"containers\n"
"- Wrapping a sub-section of a page — Wrapper contains the full page, not a "
"region"
msgstr ""
"- Building a Modal, Tray, or Drawer — those have their own layout "
"containers\n"
"- Wrapping a sub-section of a page — Wrapper contains the full page, not a "
"region"

#: css/wrapper.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- Map the main content area to a &lt;main&gt; landmark with a skip-nav link "
"so keyboard users can bypass GlobalNav\n"
"- Give ContentTabList role=\"navigation\" with a distinct aria-label such as "
"\"Page navigation\" — separate from GlobalNav's landmark\n"
"- Give TrailingContentArea role=\"complementary\" with a descriptive aria-"
"label that reflects its content, such as \"Student details\"\n"
"- Give each UtilityPanel a distinct aria-label: \"AI assistant\", "
"\"Notifications\", or \"Filters\"\n"
"- When a UtilityPanel opens, move focus into the panel; when it closes, "
"return focus to the trigger that opened it"
msgstr ""
"- Map the main content area to a &lt;main&gt; landmark with a skip-nav link "
"so keyboard users can bypass GlobalNav\n"
"- Give ContentTabList role=\"navigation\" with a distinct aria-label such as "
"\"Page navigation\" — separate from GlobalNav's landmark\n"
"- Give TrailingContentArea role=\"complementary\" with a descriptive aria-"
"label that reflects its content, such as \"Student details\"\n"
"- Give each UtilityPanel a distinct aria-label: \"AI assistant\", "
"\"Notifications\", or \"Filters\"\n"
"- When a UtilityPanel opens, move focus into the panel; when it closes, "
"return focus to the trigger that opened it"

