#: formats/components/src/functions/selectCss.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **experimental** customizable-select enhancement for `.<prefix>-simple-"
"select`. Everything is\n"
"gated behind `@supports (appearance: base-select)` (the CSS Customizable "
"Select model — Chrome 135+,\n"
"NOT yet Baseline), so it's pure progressive enhancement: browsers without "
"support keep the plain\n"
"`simpleSelectCss` control; supporting browsers get a styled "
"`::picker(select)` panel and styled\n"
"`option`s (hover/selected) from the `--instui-component-options-item-*` "
"tokens. Shipped as its own\n"
"opt-in `select.css` (like `fonts.css`) rather than folded into "
"`components.css`, precisely because the\n"
"feature is experimental — you opt in deliberately."
msgstr ""
"The **experimental** customizable-select enhancement for `.&lt;prefix&gt;-"
"simple-select`. Everything is\n"
"gated behind `@supports (appearance: base-select)` (the CSS Customizable "
"Select model — Chrome 135+,\n"
"NOT yet Baseline), so it's pure progressive enhancement: browsers without "
"support keep the plain\n"
"`simpleSelectCss` control; supporting browsers get a styled "
"`::picker(select)` panel and styled\n"
"`option`s (hover/selected) from the `--instui-component-options-item-*` "
"tokens. Shipped as its own\n"
"opt-in `select.css` (like `fonts.css`) rather than folded into "
"`components.css`, precisely because the\n"
"feature is experimental — you opt in deliberately."

#: formats/components/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/components` — an InstUI-look CSS component library, built from "
"the `--instui-*` tokens."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/components` — an InstUI-look CSS component library, built from "
"the `--instui-*` tokens."

#: formats/components/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The shipped stylesheets:"
msgstr "The shipped stylesheets:"

#: formats/components/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- **Base** ([baseCss](functions/baseCss.md)) — opt-in global document "
"defaults from the tokens (box-sizing, body\n"
"  reset, page surface, base text colour/font, `color-scheme`). It also "
"carries the focus-outline\n"
"  ring, so every focusable gets an accessible `:focus-visible` outline out "
"of the box. Load it when\n"
"  pantoken owns the page.\n"
"- **Prose** ([proseCss](functions/proseCss.md)) — styles rendered markdown/"
"prose HTML (tables, headings, links,\n"
"  lists, code) scoped to a content root, so a docs page or content region "
"looks like InstUI\n"
"  without swapping the DOM for components. This is what the site renderers "
"ship as their\n"
"  `components.css`.\n"
"- **Components** ([buttonCss](variables/buttonCss.md), [alertCss](variables/"
"alertCss.md), [badgeCss](variables/badgeCss.md), aggregated by\n"
"  [componentsCss](functions/componentsCss.md)) — class-based component "
"styles you apply to your own markup\n"
"  (`<button class=\"instui-button\">`), for the InstUI look outside a "
"component framework. The\n"
"  `--instui-elevation-*` shadow scale ([elevationCss](functions/"
"elevationCss.md)) leads this sheet, since enough\n"
"  components float that shadows are an intrinsic design attribute rather "
"than an add-on.\n"
"- **Utilities** ([viewCss](variables/viewCss.md), [spacingUtilitiesCss]"
"(variables/spacingUtilitiesCss.md), [gapCss](variables/gapCss.md), "
"[layoutUtilitiesCss](variables/layoutUtilitiesCss.md), plus a\n"
"  curated semantic-colour/token set) — an opt-in layer of cross-cutting "
"classes. The generic\n"
"  token→class emitters (`colorUtilitiesCss`, `tokenUtilitiesCss`) live in "
"`@pantoken/utils`; this\n"
"  package feeds them the curated *semantic* names, while `@pantoken/plugin-"
"primitives` feeds the raw\n"
"  palette.\n"
"- **Fonts** (opt-in `fonts.css`) — the `@font-face` rules for the "
"Instructure brand fonts. Base\n"
"  *applies* the font; `fonts.css` *loads* the woff2s, so text degrades "
"gracefully without it."
msgstr ""
"- **Base** ([baseCss](functions/baseCss.md)) — opt-in global document "
"defaults from the tokens (box-sizing, body\n"
"  reset, page surface, base text colour/font, `color-scheme`). It also "
"carries the focus-outline\n"
"  ring, so every focusable gets an accessible `:focus-visible` outline out "
"of the box. Load it when\n"
"  pantoken owns the page.\n"
"- **Prose** ([proseCss](functions/proseCss.md)) — styles rendered markdown/"
"prose HTML (tables, headings, links,\n"
"  lists, code) scoped to a content root, so a docs page or content region "
"looks like InstUI\n"
"  without swapping the DOM for components. This is what the site renderers "
"ship as their\n"
"  `components.css`.\n"
"- **Components** ([buttonCss](variables/buttonCss.md), [alertCss](variables/"
"alertCss.md), [badgeCss](variables/badgeCss.md), aggregated by\n"
"  [componentsCss](functions/componentsCss.md)) — class-based component "
"styles you apply to your own markup\n"
"  (`<button class=\"instui-button\">`), for the InstUI look outside a "
"component framework. The\n"
"  `--instui-elevation-*` shadow scale ([elevationCss](functions/"
"elevationCss.md)) leads this sheet, since enough\n"
"  components float that shadows are an intrinsic design attribute rather "
"than an add-on.\n"
"- **Utilities** ([viewCss](variables/viewCss.md), [spacingUtilitiesCss]"
"(variables/spacingUtilitiesCss.md), [gapCss](variables/gapCss.md), "
"[layoutUtilitiesCss](variables/layoutUtilitiesCss.md), plus a\n"
"  curated semantic-colour/token set) — an opt-in layer of cross-cutting "
"classes. The generic\n"
"  token→class emitters (`colorUtilitiesCss`, `tokenUtilitiesCss`) live in "
"`@pantoken/utils`; this\n"
"  package feeds them the curated *semantic* names, while `@pantoken/plugin-"
"primitives` feeds the raw\n"
"  palette.\n"
"- **Fonts** (opt-in `fonts.css`) — the `@font-face` rules for the "
"Instructure brand fonts. Base\n"
"  *applies* the font; `fonts.css` *loads* the woff2s, so text degrades "
"gracefully without it."

#: formats/components/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Everything is pure CSS derived from the token IR, so it tracks InstUI "
"through the tokens with no\n"
"dependency on the InstUI React packages. For the real, interactive "
"components, use\n"
"`@pantoken/react-markdown` (content) or `@instructure/ui-*` (apps)."
msgstr ""
"Everything is pure CSS derived from the token IR, so it tracks InstUI "
"through the tokens with no\n"
"dependency on the InstUI React packages. For the real, interactive "
"components, use\n"
"`@pantoken/react-markdown` (content) or `@instructure/ui-*` (apps)."

#: formats/components/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"This module is a barrel: each documented record lives in its own file under\n"
"`components/`/`utilities/`/`rules/`/`declarations/`, authored with the `lib/"
"` compose API. The\n"
"registries (`COMPONENTS`/`UTILITIES`/`RULES`/`DECLARATIONS`) drive "
"aggregation + the parity test."
msgstr ""
"This module is a barrel: each documented record lives in its own file under\n"
"`components/`/`utilities/`/`rules/`/`declarations/`, authored with the `lib/"
"` compose API. The\n"
"registries (`COMPONENTS`/`UTILITIES`/`RULES`/`DECLARATIONS`) drive "
"aggregation + the parity test."

