"Fires a bubbling `change` CustomEvent with `detail.value` on commit."
msgstr ""
"Wire a contenteditable field for click-to-edit commit/revert behaviour.\n"
"Enter commits, Escape reverts; blur also commits if the value changed.\n"
"Fires a bubbling `change` CustomEvent with `detail.value` on commit."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initInPlaceEdit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"  CSS:  host = .instui-in-place-edit element (which IS contenteditable)\n"
"  WC:   host = shadow .instui-in-place-edit span"
msgstr ""
"  CSS:  host = .instui-in-place-edit element (which IS contenteditable)\n"
"  WC:   host = shadow .instui-in-place-edit span"

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initModal.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Wire a CSS `<dialog class=\"instui-modal\">` or a web component's shadow\n"
"`<dialog>` to the `open` attribute protocol and `--show/--close/--toggle`\n"
"command routing. Both usages pass the same interface:"
msgstr ""
"Wire a CSS `<dialog class=\"instui-modal\">` or a web component's shadow\n"
"`<dialog>` to the `open` attribute protocol and `--show/--close/--toggle`\n"
"command routing. Both usages pass the same interface:"

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initModal.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- CSS: `host === dialog` (the dialog itself carries the id and open attr)\n"
"- WC: `host` = custom element, `dialog` = its shadow `<dialog>`"
msgstr ""
"- CSS: `host === dialog` (the dialog itself carries the id and open attr)\n"
"- WC: `host` = custom element, `dialog` = its shadow `&lt;dialog&gt;`"

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initProgressCircle.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Release a ProgressCircle's mount-animation modifier after its configured "
"delay."
msgstr ""
"Release a ProgressCircle's mount-animation modifier after its configured "
"delay."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initProgressCircle.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The delay is an explicit millisecond option or the target's computed, "
"unitless\n"
"`--animation-delay` custom property. Missing, negative, and non-finite "
"values become zero. Both the\n"
"canonical modifier and its deprecated typo alias are accepted and removed."
msgstr ""
"The delay is an explicit millisecond option or the target's computed, "
"unitless\n"
"`--animation-delay` custom property. Missing, negative, and non-finite "
"values become zero. Both the\n"
"canonical modifier and its deprecated typo alias are accepted and removed."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initRemove.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Remove a target after a timeout. Before removal, fires a cancelable, "
"bubbling `dismiss` event.\n"
"Preventing that event keeps the target mounted."
msgstr ""
"Remove a target after a timeout. Before removal, fires a cancelable, "
"bubbling `dismiss` event.\n"
"Preventing that event keeps the target mounted."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initRemove.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The timeout is an explicit millisecond option or the target's computed, "
"unitless `--timeout` CSS\n"
"custom property. Missing, non-finite, and non-positive values don't arm a "
"timer. A fade uses the\n"
"`@pantoken/components` `transition` utility's classes (`.instui-transition` "
"+ `-fade-*`), then waits\n"
"for `transitionend` (with a fallback); `transition: \"none\"` removes "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"The timeout is an explicit millisecond option or the target's computed, "
"unitless `--timeout` CSS\n"
"custom property. Missing, non-finite, and non-positive values don't arm a "
"timer. A fade uses the\n"
"`@pantoken/components` `transition` utility's classes (`.instui-transition` "
"+ `-fade-*`), then waits\n"
"for `transitionend` (with a fallback); `transition: \"none\"` removes "
"immediately."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initResponsiveOverlay.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Wire open/close commands plus width-based responsive overlay switching onto "
"a host: any\n"
"collapsible side panel (e.g. a drawer's tray) can import this interaction "
"rather than each\n"
"component reimplementing it."
msgstr ""
"Wire open/close commands plus width-based responsive overlay switching onto "
"a host: any\n"
"collapsible side panel (e.g. a drawer's tray) can import this interaction "
"rather than each\n"
"component reimplementing it."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initTooltip.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Wire hover/focus show-hide with delay onto a tooltip wrapper and its tip\n"
"bubble. Returns a cleanup function for use in web component "
"disconnectedCallback."
msgstr ""
"Wire hover/focus show-hide with delay onto a tooltip wrapper and its tip\n"
"bubble. Returns a cleanup function for use in web component "
"disconnectedCallback."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initTooltip.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"  CSS:  wrapper = .instui-tooltip element, tip = its .tip child\n"
"  WC:   wrapper = shadow .instui-tooltip, tip = shadow .tip"
msgstr ""
"  CSS:  wrapper = .instui-tooltip element, tip = its .tip child\n"
"  WC:   wrapper = shadow .instui-tooltip, tip = shadow .tip"

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initTruncateAuto.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Keep `--lines` in sync with available height for an auto-clamped truncate "
"target."
msgstr ""
"Keep `--lines` in sync with available height for an auto-clamped truncate "
"target."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/initTruncateAuto.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"- CSS usage: pass the same element as `host` and `target`.\n"
"- Web-component usage: pass custom-element host + shadow truncate target "
"span."
msgstr ""
"- CSS usage: pass the same element as `host` and `target`.\n"
"- Web-component usage: pass custom-element host + shadow truncate target "
"span."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/makeOnCommand.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Build the `command`-event router: forward a target's `command` events to a "
"handler, and where the\n"
"Invoker Commands API is missing, delegate matching `commandfor` clicks "
"across the target's tree."
msgstr ""
"Build the `command`-event router: forward a target's `command` events to a "
"handler, and where the\n"
"Invoker Commands API is missing, delegate matching `commandfor` clicks "
"across the target's tree."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/resolveSpace.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Resolve one spacing value: keyword alias to token, otherwise pass through "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Resolve one spacing value: keyword alias to token, otherwise pass through "
"unchanged."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/spacingValue.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Resolve a 1-4 value InstUI spacing shorthand (`margin`/`padding`) to its CSS "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Resolve a 1-4 value InstUI spacing shorthand (`margin`/`padding`) to its CSS "
"value."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/syncInvoker.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Mirror the host's invoker attributes onto its inner `<button>`'s IDL "
"properties, resolving ids\n"
"against the host's root so a shadow-DOM button can drive a light-DOM "
"`[popover]`/command target."
msgstr ""
"Mirror the host's invoker attributes onto its inner `&lt;button&gt;`'s IDL "
"properties, resolving ids\n"
"against the host's root so a shadow-DOM button can drive a light-DOM "
"`[popover]`/command target."

#: formats/interactions/src/functions/syncTruncateAutoLines.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Compute and apply a numeric `--lines` value from available height."
msgstr "Compute and apply a numeric `--lines` value from available height."

#: formats/interactions/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/interactions` - per-component interaction bundles for InstUI "
"components."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/interactions` - per-component interaction bundles for InstUI "
"components."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The `command`/`source` shape of an Invoker Commands `CommandEvent` (not yet "
"in DOM lib types)."
msgstr ""
"The `command`/`source` shape of an Invoker Commands `CommandEvent` (not yet "
"in DOM lib types)."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`bubbles`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"whether the event bubbles up through the DOM tree or not."
msgstr ""
"The **`bubbles`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"whether the event bubbles up through the DOM tree or not."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`cancelBubble`** property of the Event interface is deprecated. Use "
"Event.stopPropagation() instead. Setting its value to true before returning "
"from an event handler prevents propagation of the event. In later "
"implementations, setting this to false does nothing. See Browser "
"compatibility for details."
msgstr ""
"The **`cancelBubble`** property of the Event interface is deprecated. Use "
"Event.stopPropagation() instead. Setting its value to true before returning "
"from an event handler prevents propagation of the event. In later "
"implementations, setting this to false does nothing. See Browser "
"compatibility for details."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`cancelable`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"whether the event can be canceled, and therefore prevented as if the event "
"never happened."
msgstr ""
"The **`cancelable`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"whether the event can be canceled, and therefore prevented as if the event "
"never happened."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The read-only **`composed`** property of the Event interface returns a "
"boolean value which indicates whether or not the event will propagate across "
"the shadow DOM boundary into the standard DOM."
msgstr ""
"The read-only **`composed`** property of the Event interface returns a "
"boolean value which indicates whether or not the event will propagate across "
"the shadow DOM boundary into the standard DOM."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`currentTarget`** read-only property of the Event interface identifies "
"the element to which the event handler has been attached."
msgstr ""
"The **`currentTarget`** read-only property of the Event interface identifies "
"the element to which the event handler has been attached."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`defaultPrevented`** read-only property of the Event interface returns "
"a boolean value indicating whether or not the call to Event.preventDefault() "
"canceled the event."
msgstr ""
"The **`defaultPrevented`** read-only property of the Event interface returns "
"a boolean value indicating whether or not the call to Event.preventDefault() "
"canceled the event."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`eventPhase`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"which phase of the event flow is currently being evaluated."
msgstr ""
"The **`eventPhase`** read-only property of the Event interface indicates "
"which phase of the event flow is currently being evaluated."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`isTrusted`** read-only property of the Event interface is a boolean "
"value that is true when the event was generated by the user agent (including "
"via user actions and programmatic methods such as HTMLElement.focus()), and "
"false when the event was dispatched via EventTarget.dispatchEvent(). The "
"only exception is the click event, which initializes the isTrusted property "
"to false in user agents."
msgstr ""
"The **`isTrusted`** read-only property of the Event interface is a boolean "
"value that is true when the event was generated by the user agent (including "
"via user actions and programmatic methods such as HTMLElement.focus()), and "
"false when the event was dispatched via EventTarget.dispatchEvent(). The "
"only exception is the click event, which initializes the isTrusted property "
"to false in user agents."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The Event property **`returnValue`** indicates whether the default action "
"for this event has been prevented or not."
msgstr ""
"The Event property **`returnValue`** indicates whether the default action "
"for this event has been prevented or not."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The deprecated **`Event.srcElement`** is an alias for the Event.target "
"property. Use Event.target instead."
msgstr ""
"The deprecated **`Event.srcElement`** is an alias for the Event.target "
"property. Use Event.target instead."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The read-only **`target`** property of the Event interface is a reference to "
"the object onto which the event was dispatched. It is different from "
"Event.currentTarget when the event handler is called during the bubbling or "
"capturing phase of the event."
msgstr ""
"The read-only **`target`** property of the Event interface is a reference to "
"the object onto which the event was dispatched. It is different from "
"Event.currentTarget when the event handler is called during the bubbling or "
"capturing phase of the event."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`timeStamp`** read-only property of the Event interface returns the "
"time (in milliseconds) at which the event was created."
msgstr ""
"The **`timeStamp`** read-only property of the Event interface returns the "
"time (in milliseconds) at which the event was created."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`type`** read-only property of the Event interface returns a string "
"containing the event's type. It is set when the event is constructed and is "
"the name commonly used to refer to the specific event, such as click, load, "
"or error."
msgstr ""
"The **`type`** read-only property of the Event interface returns a string "
"containing the event's type. It is set when the event is constructed and is "
"the name commonly used to refer to the specific event, such as click, load, "
"or error."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`composedPath()`** method of the Event interface returns the event's "
"path which is an array of the objects on which listeners will be invoked. "
"This does not include nodes in shadow trees if the shadow root was created "
"with its ShadowRoot.mode closed."
msgstr ""
"The **`composedPath()`** method of the Event interface returns the event's "
"path which is an array of the objects on which listeners will be invoked. "
"This does not include nodes in shadow trees if the shadow root was created "
"with its ShadowRoot.mode closed."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`Event.initEvent()`** method is used to initialize the value of an "
"event created using Document.createEvent()."
msgstr ""
"The **`Event.initEvent()`** method is used to initialize the value of an "
"event created using Document.createEvent()."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`preventDefault()`** method of the Event interface tells the user "
"agent that the event is being explicitly handled, so its default action, "
"such as page scrolling, link navigation, or pasting text, should not be "
"taken."
msgstr ""
"The **`preventDefault()`** method of the Event interface tells the user "
"agent that the event is being explicitly handled, so its default action, "
"such as page scrolling, link navigation, or pasting text, should not be "
"taken."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`stopImmediatePropagation()`** method of the Event interface prevents "
"other listeners of the same event from being called."
msgstr ""
"The **`stopImmediatePropagation()`** method of the Event interface prevents "
"other listeners of the same event from being called."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#: renderers/web-components/src/interfaces/CommandEventish.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The **`stopPropagation()`** method of the Event interface prevents further "
"propagation of the current event in the capturing and bubbling phases. It "
"does not, however, prevent any default behaviors from occurring; for "
"instance, clicks on links are still processed. If you want to stop those "
"behaviors, see the preventDefault() method. It also does not prevent "
"propagation to other event-handlers of the current element. If you want to "
"stop those, see stopImmediatePropagation()."
msgstr ""
"The **`stopPropagation()`** method of the Event interface prevents further "
"propagation of the current event in the capturing and bubbling phases. It "
"does not, however, prevent any default behaviors from occurring; for "
"instance, clicks on links are still processed. If you want to stop those "
"behaviors, see the preventDefault() method. It also does not prevent "
"propagation to other event-handlers of the current element. If you want to "
"stop those, see stopImmediatePropagation()."

#: formats/interactions/src/interfaces/ProgressCircleHandle.md
