#: packages/utils/src/functions/colorUtilitiesCss.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Build the semantic-colour utility stylesheet: `.<prefix>-bg-<name>` "
"(background),\n"
"`.<prefix>-text-<name>` (text colour), `.<prefix>-border-<name>` (border "
"colour), one per semantic\n"
"colour token. `.<prefix>-color-<name>` is emitted alongside `.<prefix>-text-"
"<name>` as an alias — same\n"
"declaration, either class name works. Overrides are therefore only ever "
"token-valid — no primitives,\n"
"no arbitrary hex. Pass the token names per family (e.g. from `@pantoken/"
"tokens`), or an explicit\n"
"`[name, token]` pair to source a name from a different token than the "
"family's own scale."
msgstr ""
"Build the semantic-colour utility stylesheet: `.&lt;prefix&gt;-bg-"
"&lt;name&gt;` (background),\n"
"`.&lt;prefix&gt;-text-&lt;name&gt;` (text colour), `.&lt;prefix&gt;-border-"
"&lt;name&gt;` (border colour), one per semantic\n"
"colour token. `.&lt;prefix&gt;-color-&lt;name&gt;` is emitted alongside "
"`.&lt;prefix&gt;-text-&lt;name&gt;` as an alias — same\n"
"declaration, either class name works. Overrides are therefore only ever "
"token-valid — no primitives,\n"
"no arbitrary hex. Pass the token names per family (e.g. from `@pantoken/"
"tokens`), or an explicit\n"
"`[name, token]` pair to source a name from a different token than the "
"family's own scale."

