#: packages/utils/src/functions/tokenUtilitiesCss.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Build token-driven utility classes: one class per token, applying it to its "
"natural CSS property. The\n"
"token's `--instui-` tail is the class name, so `--instui-font-weight-body-"
"strong` under property\n"
"`font-weight` yields\n"
"`.<prefix>-font-weight-body-strong { font-weight: var(--instui-font-weight-"
"body-strong); }`. Use it for\n"
"every \"one token → one property\" family (font-family/weight, line-height, "
"border-radius, border-width,\n"
"opacity, box-shadow). Colour and spacing keep their own builders — one token "
"maps to several\n"
"properties there. Pass the token names per property (e.g. filtered from "
"`@pantoken/tokens`)."
msgstr ""
"Build token-driven utility classes: one class per token, applying it to its "
"natural CSS property. The\n"
"token's `--instui-` tail is the class name, so `--instui-font-weight-body-"
"strong` under property\n"
"`font-weight` yields\n"
"`.&lt;prefix&gt;-font-weight-body-strong { font-weight: var(--instui-font-"
"weight-body-strong); }`. Use it for\n"
"every \"one token → one property\" family (font-family/weight, line-height, "
"border-radius, border-width,\n"
"opacity, box-shadow). Colour and spacing keep their own builders — one token "
"maps to several\n"
"properties there. Pass the token names per property (e.g. filtered from "
"`@pantoken/tokens`)."

