#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* "
"`surface`. This is the CSS-only\n"
"form of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand "
"button, a\n"
"primary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a "
"fixed inverse token,\n"
"it picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the "
"surface changes."
msgstr ""
"The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* "
"`surface`. This is the CSS-only\n"
"form of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand "
"button, a\n"
"primary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a "
"fixed inverse token,\n"
"it picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the "
"surface changes."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and "
"snaps it to `0` (black) or\n"
"`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no "
"JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr ""
"It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and "
"snaps it to `0` (black) or\n"
"`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no "
"JS, no fixed hex."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
