msgstr "How much of `overlay` shows through, 0–100 (default `50`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI "
"`@instructure/ui-color-utils`\n"
"helpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI "
"`@instructure/ui-color-utils`\n"
"helpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex "
"values. pantoken emits\n"
"`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through "
"`light-dark()`), so the\n"
"math has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string "
"built from\n"
"[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-"
"mix) and\n"
"[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/"
"CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\n"
"both Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the "
"token even when it's a\n"
"scheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-"
"code a derived shade."
msgstr ""
"InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex "
"values. pantoken emits\n"
"`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through "
"`light-dark()`), so the\n"
"math has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string "
"built from\n"
"[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-"
"mix) and\n"
"[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/"
"CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\n"
"both Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the "
"token even when it's a\n"
"scheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-"
"code a derived shade."

