#: plugins/pantoken/deprecations/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/plugin-deprecations` — lifecycle-aware compatibility shims for "
"dropped upstream tokens."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/plugin-deprecations` — lifecycle-aware compatibility shims for "
"dropped upstream tokens."

#: plugins/pantoken/deprecations/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"When an upstream release drops a `--instui-*` token, a hand-authored "
"`DeprecationLedger`\n"
"records its lifecycle: when it was deprecated, the upstream minor that will "
"remove it, and how to\n"
"keep it working meanwhile — either forward to a canonical token "
"(`replacement` → `var(...)`) or\n"
"freeze its last-known literal (`value`). This plugin appends one shim token "
"per entry. Because the\n"
"shim is a single `var(...)` or a plain value, `defineToken` records its "
"`refersTo`/syntax and\n"
"`toCss` emits it, so the shim rides into css/scss/less/stylus/wordpress/"
"vanilla with no extra wiring."
msgstr ""
"When an upstream release drops a `--instui-*` token, a hand-authored "
"`DeprecationLedger`\n"
"records its lifecycle: when it was deprecated, the upstream minor that will "
"remove it, and how to\n"
"keep it working meanwhile — either forward to a canonical token "
"(`replacement` → `var(...)`) or\n"
"freeze its last-known literal (`value`). This plugin appends one shim token "
"per entry. Because the\n"
"shim is a single `var(...)` or a plain value, `defineToken` records its "
"`refersTo`/syntax and\n"
"`toCss` emits it, so the shim rides into css/scss/less/stylus/wordpress/"
"vanilla with no extra wiring."

#: plugins/pantoken/deprecations/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The retirement is enforced elsewhere (the upgrade pipeline hard-fails a bump "
"once an entry's\n"
"`removeIn` upstream minor is reached, forcing the entry to be retired and a "
"consumer minor cut).\n"
"[dueForRemoval](functions/dueForRemoval.md) is the check that powers it; "
"[describeLifecycle](functions/describeLifecycle.md) powers the docs."
msgstr ""
"The retirement is enforced elsewhere (the upgrade pipeline hard-fails a bump "
"once an entry's\n"
"`removeIn` upstream minor is reached, forcing the entry to be retired and a "
"consumer minor cut).\n"
"[dueForRemoval](functions/dueForRemoval.md) is the check that powers it; "
"[describeLifecycle](functions/describeLifecycle.md) powers the docs."

