#: plugins/typedoc/demo/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/typedoc-plugin-demo` — a TypeDoc plugin for the `@demo` block tag."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/typedoc-plugin-demo` — a TypeDoc plugin for the `@demo` block tag."

#: plugins/typedoc/demo/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Authors attach a live, embeddable demo to any symbol with `@demo <spec>`, "
"where `<spec>` is either\n"
"a bare URL or a `<provider>:<ref>` pair (for example `stackblitz:abc123`, "
"`codesandbox:xy12z`,\n"
"`wp-playground:https://…/blueprint.json`, or `self:button`). This plugin "
"registers nothing about\n"
"providers itself — it stays deliberately dumb and reusable: it moves each "
"`@demo` tag's spec into\n"
"a fenced `demo` block appended to the symbol's summary, and your docs "
"renderer decides how to\n"
"turn a spec into an iframe. (See `@pantoken/demo` for a renderer that "
"resolves the providers.)"
msgstr ""
"Authors attach a live, embeddable demo to any symbol with `@demo "
"&lt;spec&gt;`, where `&lt;spec&gt;` is either\n"
"a bare URL or a `&lt;provider&gt;:&lt;ref&gt;` pair (for example "
"`stackblitz:abc123`, `codesandbox:xy12z`,\n"
"`wp-playground:https://…/blueprint.json`, or `self:button`). This plugin "
"registers nothing about\n"
"providers itself — it stays deliberately dumb and reusable: it moves each "
"`@demo` tag's spec into\n"
"a fenced `demo` block appended to the symbol's summary, and your docs "
"renderer decides how to\n"
