#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/vite-workspace-orchestrator` — a Vite dev-server plugin that "
"watches upstream workspace\n"
"packages and rebuilds them (and their dependents) when source changes."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/vite-workspace-orchestrator` — a Vite dev-server plugin that "
"watches upstream workspace\n"
"packages and rebuilds them (and their dependents) when source changes."

#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"During development, changes to a local workspace package normally need a "
"manual rebuild before the\n"
"dev server reflects them. This plugin automates that: it watches each "
"upstream package's source\n"
"with native `fs.watch` (not Vite's chokidar, which filters paths outside the "
"project root),\n"
"debounces rapid changes, rebuilds in topological order, and registers built "
"output with Vite's\n"
"watcher so the browser reloads. In pantoken's docs it keeps the generated "
"CSS (`@pantoken/css`,\n"
"`@pantoken/components`) fresh as you edit the libraries, instead of only at "
"build time."
msgstr ""
"During development, changes to a local workspace package normally need a "
"manual rebuild before the\n"
"dev server reflects them. This plugin automates that: it watches each "
"upstream package's source\n"
"with native `fs.watch` (not Vite's chokidar, which filters paths outside the "
"project root),\n"
"debounces rapid changes, rebuilds in topological order, and registers built "
"output with Vite's\n"
"watcher so the browser reloads. In pantoken's docs it keeps the generated "
"CSS (`@pantoken/css`,\n"
"`@pantoken/components`) fresh as you edit the libraries, instead of only at "
"build time."

#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It applies during `serve` only, so production builds are untouched."
msgstr "It applies during `serve` only, so production builds are untouched."

