#: renderers/foundation/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Foundation is Sass-first, so this package ships two layers. "
"[toFoundationSettings](functions/toFoundationSettings.md) emits a\n"
"`_settings`-style Sass partial that points Foundation's setting variables at "
"`var(--instui-*)`, so\n"
"a Sass build compiles the Instructure look while keeping runtime theming "
"through the same custom\n"
"properties. [toFoundationCss](functions/toFoundationCss.md) emits a thin CSS "
"overlay that themes the common compiled\n"
"classes (`.button`, `.callout`, links) the same way — useful when you "
"consume stock Foundation CSS\n"
"and just want to layer Instructure colors on top without recompiling."
msgstr ""
"Foundation is Sass-first, so this package ships two layers. "
"[toFoundationSettings](functions/toFoundationSettings.md) emits a\n"
"`_settings`-style Sass partial that points Foundation's setting variables at "
"`var(--instui-*)`, so\n"
"a Sass build compiles the Instructure look while keeping runtime theming "
"through the same custom\n"
"properties. [toFoundationCss](functions/toFoundationCss.md) emits a thin CSS "
"overlay that themes the common compiled\n"
"classes (`.button`, `.callout`, links) the same way — useful when you "
"consume stock Foundation CSS\n"
"and just want to layer Instructure colors on top without recompiling."

