msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/markdown-it` — a markdown-it plugin that renders `:icon:` codes "
"as inline SVG and\n"
"standalone color values (`#03893D`, `rgb(…)`, `oklch(…)`) as swatches, using "
"the pantoken icon\n"
"set."
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/markdown-it` — a markdown-it plugin that renders `:icon:` codes "
"as inline SVG and\n"
"standalone color values (`#03893D`, `rgb(…)`, `oklch(…)`) as swatches, using "
"the pantoken icon\n"
"set."

#: renderers/markdown-it/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"It ports the `@pantoken/rehype` and `@pantoken/react-markdown` pipelines "
"onto markdown-it: a\n"
"single core rule walks each inline token's text children, splits them on the "
"icon and color\n"
"patterns, and swaps the matches for `html_inline` tokens. Icon codes resolve "
"through a chain —\n"
"plugin `rehype` resolvers first, then an explicit [MarkdownItOptions.resolve]"
"(interfaces/MarkdownItOptions.md#resolve), then the\n"
"built-in `@pantoken/icons` set — so brand-icon plugins compose the same way "
"they do elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"It ports the `@pantoken/rehype` and `@pantoken/react-markdown` pipelines "
"onto markdown-it: a\n"
"single core rule walks each inline token's text children, splits them on the "
"icon and color\n"
"patterns, and swaps the matches for `html_inline` tokens. Icon codes resolve "
"through a chain —\n"
"plugin `rehype` resolvers first, then an explicit [MarkdownItOptions.resolve]"
"(interfaces/MarkdownItOptions.md#resolve), then the\n"
"built-in `@pantoken/icons` set — so brand-icon plugins compose the same way "
"they do elsewhere."

#: renderers/markdown-it/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"The emitted markup uses the same class names as the other renderers "
"(`pantoken-icon`,\n"
"`pantoken-color-swatch`), so loading `@pantoken/components` styles it. Wrap "
"the rendered HTML in a\n"
"`.pantoken-prose` container (see [PROSE\\_CLASS](variables/PROSE_CLASS.md)) "
"to pick up the prose layer too."
msgstr ""
"The emitted markup uses the same class names as the other renderers "
"(`pantoken-icon`,\n"
"`pantoken-color-swatch`), so loading `@pantoken/components` styles it. Wrap "
"the rendered HTML in a\n"
"`.pantoken-prose` container (see [PROSE\\_CLASS](variables/PROSE_CLASS.md)) "
"to pick up the prose layer too."

