#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"Build the shared [RegisterContext](../interfaces/RegisterContext.md) a "
"`register()`-style call threads to every element's\n"
"`define`. The icon resolver is injectable: `register()` always passes the "
"real,\n"
"`@pantoken/icons`-backed [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) (unchanged default behavior "
"for every existing caller),\n"
"while the per-element CDN build passes [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) for "
"elements that never call it —\n"
"`@pantoken/icons`/`@pantoken/tokens` is a multi-MB dependency, and since "
"Rollup can't code-split\n"
"`iife`/`umd` output, anything statically reachable from a bundle's entry "
"ends up in the whole\n"
"bundle, regardless of whether that specific element's code path ever invokes "
"it. This module has no\n"
"top-level side effects for exactly that reason — importing it (unlike "
"importing `../index.ts`, which\n"
"auto-registers everything on import) never reaches [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) "
"unless the caller passes it in."
msgstr ""
"Build the shared [RegisterContext](../interfaces/RegisterContext.md) a "
"`register()`-style call threads to every element's\n"
"`define`. The icon resolver is injectable: `register()` always passes the "
"real,\n"
"`@pantoken/icons`-backed [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) (unchanged default behavior "
"for every existing caller),\n"
"while the per-element CDN build passes [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) for "
"elements that never call it —\n"
"`@pantoken/icons`/`@pantoken/tokens` is a multi-MB dependency, and since "
"Rollup can't code-split\n"
"`iife`/`umd` output, anything statically reachable from a bundle's entry "
"ends up in the whole\n"
"bundle, regardless of whether that specific element's code path ever invokes "
"it. This module has no\n"
"top-level side effects for exactly that reason — importing it (unlike "
"importing `../index.ts`, which\n"
"auto-registers everything on import) never reaches [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) "
"unless the caller passes it in."

