#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`<instui-calendar>` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is "
"the selected day and\n"
"`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons "
"and every day are\n"
"`<button>`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-"
"next`,\n"
"`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and "
"dispatches a composed,\n"
"bubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own "
"grid (no slot), so it\n"
"works standalone or nested inside a date picker."
msgstr ""
"`&lt;instui-calendar&gt;` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-"
"dd`) is the selected day and\n"
"`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons "
"and every day are\n"
"`&lt;button&gt;`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--"
"calendar-next`,\n"
"`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and "
"dispatches a composed,\n"
"bubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own "
"grid (no slot), so it\n"
"works standalone or nested inside a date picker."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`<instui-context-view>` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is "
"a native `[popover]`\n"
"(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button "
"can toggle it by id.\n"
"Position it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; "
"otherwise it centres in\n"
"the top layer. Content goes in the default slot."
msgstr ""
"`&lt;instui-context-view&gt;` — a callout surface with a caret. The host "
"itself is a native `[popover]`\n"
"(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button "
"can toggle it by id.\n"
"Position it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; "
"otherwise it centres in\n"
"the top layer. Content goes in the default slot."

