msgstr "`@pantoken/demo` — the render side of the `@demo` system."

#: tools/demo/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"`@pantoken/typedoc-plugin-demo` turns a `@demo <spec>` tag into a fenced "
"`demo` block whose\n"
"body is the spec (a bare URL or a `<provider>:<ref>` pair). This package "
"resolves that spec into an\n"
"embeddable iframe and renders the surrounding panel — an MDN-style \"live "
"sample.\""
msgstr ""
"`@pantoken/typedoc-plugin-demo` turns a `@demo &lt;spec&gt;` tag into a "
"fenced `demo` block whose\n"
"body is the spec (a bare URL or a `&lt;provider&gt;:&lt;ref&gt;` pair). This "
"package resolves that spec into an\n"
"embeddable iframe and renders the surrounding panel — an MDN-style \"live "
"sample.\""

#: tools/demo/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid ""
"It ships three things: [resolveDemo](functions/resolveDemo.md) (spec → "
"iframe attributes, framework-agnostic), a\n"
"markdown-it plugin ([demoMarkdownIt](functions/demoMarkdownIt.md)) that "
"turns `demo` fences into the panel HTML, and a\n"
"self-hosted runner (`@pantoken/demo/runner.html`) — a same-origin page that "
"fetches a bare\n"
"HTML/CSS/JS demo and renders it with your token stylesheets injected, so "
"`self:` demos need no\n"
"third-party account and no framing workarounds."
msgstr ""
"It ships three things: [resolveDemo](functions/resolveDemo.md) (spec → "
"iframe attributes, framework-agnostic), a\n"
"markdown-it plugin ([demoMarkdownIt](functions/demoMarkdownIt.md)) that "
"turns `demo` fences into the panel HTML, and a\n"
"self-hosted runner (`@pantoken/demo/runner.html`) — a same-origin page that "
"fetches a bare\n"
"HTML/CSS/JS demo and renders it with your token stylesheets injected, so "
"`self:` demos need no\n"
"third-party account and no framing workarounds."

